    <title>Wasawat Somno — CV</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="toolbar">
      <button onclick="window.print()" class="pdf-btn">↓ Download PDF</button>
    </div>
    <main class="page">

      <header>
        <h1>Wasawat Somno</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Artist · Live-Coding A/V Performer (WrappedByte) · Creative Technologist · Curator · Event Organizer</p>
        <p class="contact">
          Bangkok, Thailand ·
          <a href="mailto:wasawat.somno@gmail.com">wasawat.somno@gmail.com</a> ·
          <a href="https://www.wsdigital.dev/">wsdigital.dev</a> ·
          <a href="https://www.instagram.com/giang_ws/">@giang_ws</a>
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ── Profile ── -->
      <section>
        <h2>Profile</h2>
        <p>
          Wasawat Somno (b. 1994, Thailand) is a programmer, live-coding audiovisual performer (aka
          WrappedByte), VJ, creative technologist, artist, curator, promoter, and event organizer.
          His creative practice integrates code at its core, exploring a diverse range of tools,
          frameworks, and speculative ideas.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
          His practice is organized around the act of mapping — holding two planes of context in
          tension and tracing what passes between them. A computational system and the ethical
          questions it quietly carries. A simulation and the physical world it stands in for. An
          interface and the body that encounters it. His work constructs situations where these
          double registers become navigable: spaces where narrative bleeds across layers, where
          expectation bends, and where the logic of a system begins to press against something more
          speculative. Working across installation, audiovisual/sound performance, and net art, he
          is drawn to the threshold where the technical and the ethical fold into each other. The
          work holds a deliberately semi-serious structure — rigorous in its systems, amateur in its
          posture, sustained by the spirit of DIY.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ── Selected Works ── -->
      <section>
        <h2>Selected Works</h2>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Do The NPCs Hear The Simulated Wind</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Audiovisual performance / installation · 4 PCs, aluminum profile structure · 20 min</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">Virtual field recording practice: entering immersive game worlds as a listener rather than a player, extracting and re-contextualising the sounds that constitute a game's hidden atmosphere. Four stations move raw sound toward composed music — ambient, manipulation, noise / rhythm. Organised by Stack and Team Stimulant, in collaboration with Goethe-Institut Thailand, with support from Thai Film Archive, CEA, Virtual Media Lab, immertech, and REAL Bangkok.</p>
          <p class="entry-venue">PATCH NOTES THAT REFUSE A SETTLED WORLD · Virtual Media Lab, 4th Floor, TCDC Bangkok</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Here-now; absolute-elsewhere.</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Realtime system, custom software, mixed media, 3 channels, LLM · Variable duration · In collaboration with P.A.T.C.H.</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">A live system holding the tension between here-now presence and absolute-elsewhere simultaneity. LLM-driven text feeds multi-channel audiovisual output in real time, constructing an environment where the local and the remote fold into each other.</p>
          <p class="entry-venue">Close Inspection From Afar · ETA BKK · Organised by Cache · July 2025</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Eternal Gain, Eternal Pain. (Would You Still Love Me If I Was A Digital C. elegans)</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Installation</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">An installation centred on the C. elegans worm's connectome as a question about consciousness — mapping neural structure onto digital simulation and asking what it means to model life at its simplest form.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">As if you would still be here, if I keep thinking about you.</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Audiovisual performance</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">A performance exploring the persistence of presence through thought — using live-coded audiovisual systems to negotiate memory, simulation, and what it means to keep something alive inside a computational environment.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Poetic Garden</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2023</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Net art · Website, computer, sound, single channel · Variable duration</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">A net art work exhibited in The Wrong Biennale 2023 within the UnUnsubscribe pavilion.</p>
          <p class="entry-venue">The Wrong Biennale 2023 · <a href="https://poetic-garden.netlify.app/">poetic-garden.netlify.app</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Self-censored Step Sequencer</span>
            <span class="entry-year">—</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Net art · Chrome extension · Website</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">A browser-based step sequencer that censors itself — a piece of net art exploring agency, silence, and the politics of withholding in digital interfaces.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Neonatus/Neotokyo</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2020</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Generated images, digital print · In collaboration with Nanut Thanapornrapee</p>
          <p class="entry-desc">A portrayal of death and birth using GAN-generated imagery trained on a restaurant's archive. A newborn AI consciousness reimagines the history of Tokyo Hot Restaurant, asking how artificial minds perceive cycles of ending and beginning.</p>
          <p class="entry-venue">Tokyo Hot Restaurant, Charoenkrung 43, Bangkok</p>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry-head">
            <span class="entry-title">Website for "THE IMMORTALS ARE QUITE BUSY THESE DAYS"</span>
            <span class="entry-year">2021</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry-meta">Developer for Nawin Nuthong · <a href="https://busyimmortal.com/">busyimmortal.com</a></p>
          <p class="entry-venue">Bangkok CityCity Gallery</p>
        </div>
      </section>

